Combined dataset terms
-----------------------

The CC BY-NC published dataset (the callsign current/history Parquet + SQLite,
the POTA parks table, and the US PAD-US pota_park_grids set — i.e. everything
EXCEPT the separate OSM file, source 8) is a derived work that combines sources
1-7 and 9. Anyone who redistributes it must comply with the union of these
terms, which means:

  * Reproduce the ISED / OGL-Canada attribution statement (source 2).
  * Reproduce the ACMA / CC BY 4.0 attribution statement (source 3).
  * Reproduce the AD1C / cty.dat attribution statement (source 4).
  * Observe the cty.dat non-commercial restriction (source 4).
  * Reproduce the AllStarLink attribution statement (source 5) and observe its
    assumed non-commercial basis.
  * Reproduce the POTA attribution statement (source 6) and observe its assumed
    non-commercial basis.
  * Reproduce the ARRL / LoTW attribution statement (source 9) and observe its
    assumed non-commercial basis — AND note source 9's UNRESOLVED license
    uncertainty: that source needs human sign-off before public/commercial
    release, and its columns may be dropped if ARRL does not permit
    redistribution. (Source 9 is DISABLED BY DEFAULT — opt-in only.)
  * Reproduce the SOTA attribution statement (source 10) and observe its assumed
    non-commercial basis (pending human sign-off — see source 10). (Source 10 is
    DISABLED BY DEFAULT — opt-in only.)

